v3.2.28
Radon Player 3.2.28: The DJ, on air
## 3.2.28: The DJ, on air (Windows and Android)
- **The DJ plays from your whole library:** instead of picking a playlist, folder or album for it, the DJ now always plays from every song in your library as one group: your own files, your downloads and saved songs, and every song in your playlists, streams too (with Include new songs, new ones like what you listen to as well). It no longer has to switch between groups of songs, and its sets all draw on the one library. The DJ button on playlists and albums, and the DJ's From menu, are gone.
- **Artist spotlight goes through your whole library:** it only ever picked from your 25 most played artists, so the same few came up often. Now any artist with five or more songs in your library can have the spotlight (the ones you play more a little likelier), and an artist isn't picked again until most of the others have had a turn.
- **Never skipped is now Not skipped this month:** a song you skipped once (not in the mood, say) was out of the DJ's Never skipped set for good, so in time there'd be none left. The set now goes by this month: only songs you've played this month and heard to the end every time they came on (the last 30 days early in the month, while there are few plays yet), and each month they all count again. The more times you've heard one out (and the fewer times you've ever skipped it), the likelier it is to come up. Skips (Your music › Skips) is just as it was.
- **The DJ's mood facts take turns:** she nearly always told you about your top mood. Now she also tells you about the others, a mood picked at random each time: how much of your listening it is, how many plays it has, and how many this month.
- **The DJ talks over the music, like a radio DJ:** she used to talk between songs, the song held silent (or played under her muted and then started again from the top) until she was done, and when her voice was slow to come the music sat frozen. Now the music never waits for her: the song plays on from the moment it's due, turned down under her voice while she talks and eased back up after, never paused and never started again. Bit-perfect to a USB DAC, her voice is mixed into the stream with the music turned down under it (the music only stops for her when it isn't playing at all, before the first song, say). A line whose voice doesn't come within 15 seconds is left unsaid.

### Good to know
- **Android:** install RadonPlayer-Next.apk over Radon Player Next (same app, same signature: your library, settings and stats stay), or tap Update in Settings.
- **Windows:** Radon-Player-3.2.28.msi installs over 3.2.27, or use Update in Settings.
